PRIOR ART (ideas and published numbers; no code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------
fakeflac — MIT — Copyright (c) 2022 Maurits van der Schee
  https://github.com/mevdschee/fakeflac
  The cutoff search in src/analyze.ts follows its method: average the
  spectrum, smooth it, walk down from the top of the band and look for a
  steep step. The code here is written from scratch in TypeScript.

FLAC Detective — MIT — Guillain-RDCDE
  https://github.com/Guillain-RDCDE/FLAC_Detective
  The habit of wording verdicts as evidence ("suspicious") instead of a flat
  "fake", because a wrong accusation costs more than a miss.

Spek — GPL-3.0 — Alexander Kojevnikov
  https://github.com/alexkay/spek
  The idea of judging a file by its spectrogram. No Spek code is used.

LAME — LGPL — The LAME Project
  https://lame.sourceforge.io
  The table of default low-pass frequencies per bitrate in src/analyze.ts
  comes from libmp3lame/lame.c (optimum_bandwidth). Only the numbers are
  used, as facts about how the encoder behaves. No LAME code is used.

FLAC format — Xiph.Org Foundation
  https://xiph.org/flac/format.html
  The layout of the STREAMINFO block (sample count, audio MD5).

